<string name="help1">Create a token from Developer settings, then Personal access tokens, Fine-grained tokens, and Generate new token.</string>
<string name="help2">Upload permissions: Contents = Read and write and Metadata = Read-only. For new repositories use Administration = Read and write.</string>
<string name="help3">Limit the token to the repositories it needs. Never share it; revoke it from GitHub when necessary.</string>
<string name="help4">Smart upload compares Git SHAs, so unchanged files are not uploaded again.</string>
<string name="help5">If the connection drops, the app keeps the ZIP and retries automatically when the connection returns.</string>
<string name="help6">You can cancel at any time. The pending ZIP is retained when WorkManager stops the job unexpectedly.</string>
<string name="help7">ZIP is the only upload source. You can send a ZIP from your file manager share menu.</string>
<string name="help8">Changed files are uploaded in parallel while the ZIP is processed in bounded batches.</string>
<string name="help9">Auto-naming uses the ZIP filename as the new repository name.</string>
<string name="help10">Download saves a ZIP copy of the selected repository branch.</string>
<string name="help11">Add an ignore file to the ZIP to exclude files or folders from upload.</string>
